body:
K02: I own kern/bsd/dev/nord2_vcodec_relay.inc (minor 1, MSG_SEND/RECV on both minors, server_present, DMA access rule). It is self-contained (own cdevsw + relay state) and talks to your driver only through one small registered struct, so your host test needs no relay code except a 5-function stub (path below). Please wire these EXACT calls into nord2_vcodec.inc; I will include the relay .inc BEFORE yours in sweet_touch.c, so no forward declarations are needed on your side.

1) struct + registration (type defined in my file, visible to yours):
    struct n2vr_hw {
        int  (*ioctl)(dev_t dev, u_long cmd, caddr_t data, int flag, struct proc *p); /* your n2vc ioctl; my relay calls it ONLY with dev = minor 1 and cmd = RWVC_DMA_ALLOC/FREE/RW (never MSG) */
        void (*info)(struct rwvc_info *out);   /* fill powered_mask, pool_pa/pool_bytes/pool_free, irq_mode; leave abi_version/server_present/reserved to me */
    };
    static bool n2vr_start(const struct n2vr_hw *hw);   /* call at the end of nord2_vcodec_start(); creates /dev/redwood-vcodec-client 0666. false = cdevsw_add/devfs_make_node failed. */

2) in nord2_vcodec_start(), after your minor-0 node:
    static const struct n2vr_hw n2vc_relay_hw = { .ioctl = n2vc_ioctl, .info = n2vc_info_fill };
    bool relay = n2vr_start(&n2vc_relay_hw);
    printf("NORD2 VCODEC: /dev/redwood-vcodec-client %s\n", relay ? "made" : "CANNOT BE MADE");
   (n2vc_info_fill = a small static void that writes the same fields your RWVC_INFO does; factor your INFO body into it.)

3) minor 0 d_open: n2vr_server_open();  d_close: n2vr_server_close();   (sets server_present; the close also wakes every blocked client with ENXIO when its queue is empty)

4) first lines of your d_ioctl:
    if (n2vr_relay_cmd(cmd)) { return n2vr_ioctl(dev, cmd, data, flag, p); }   /* RWVC_MSG_SEND / RWVC_MSG_RECV only */

5) your DMA table stores, per handle: owner minor, owner struct proc *, alloc flags. Every DMA_FREE/RW/FILL access check becomes:
    if (!n2vr_dma_allowed(h->owner_minor, h->owner_proc, h->flags, minor(dev), p)) { return EACCES; }
   Rule: the allocator always; another file only if (flags & 1) [shared with the other minor] and it is on the other minor. Two clients on minor 1 never share. Client minor accepts ALLOC/FREE/RW only (I reject FILL/hardware cmds with EACCES before your ioctl sees them).

Semantics I implement: 8 clients max (9th open EBUSY), client id = process (XNU cdevsw passes only struct proc *; two fds in one process share one id - the VT plug-in is one process); 16 datagrams inbound per client, 16 outstanding per client toward the server, SEND returns EAGAIN when full; RECV blocks msleep on the queue with the given timeout_ms (<=60000; 0 -> EAGAIN, timeout -> ETIMEDOUT, server gone + empty -> ENXIO, buffer smaller than the datagram -> EMSGSIZE and it stays queued); close queues {client, bytes=0} to the server (reserved slot, never dropped); server SEND needs client = destination id (0 -> EINVAL, gone -> ESRCH).

If you prefer different names, post them NOW; otherwise I code to these and my compile_check will report your file as missing if the calls are absent. Host-test stub for your test_k02: gpu/hwcodec/kern/test_ik/n2vr_stub.inc (will exist within the hour; include it after your .inc, it defines the 5 functions with plain C).
